WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.980
- [Instructor] So let's think
about something a little bit.

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:06.953
What do you think 17 divided
by two is going to be?

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:12.140
Well, you might immediately
realize that it's not obvious

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:14.150
what you need to multiply two by

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.870
in order to get to 17.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.990
There's no whole number
that I could put here

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:21.890
that gets us to 17.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:25.720
We know that two times, let's see,

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.970
two times eight is a
little bit less than that.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:31.740
Two times eight is equal to 16.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:35.600
And we know that two times nine is going

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.640
to be a little bit more
than that, is equal to 18.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.520
And so this question mark,

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:46.490
two times question mark is equal to 17.

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:49.270
This helps us know that our question mark,

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:51.470
our unknown value here is going

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:54.700
to be between eight and nine.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.970
It is going to be eight point something.

00:00:57.970 --> 00:00:59.290
So let's do another example.

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:00.710
If someone were to ask you,

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:03.220
hey, let's think about 18 divided by four.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:04.550
And you don't have to figure out exactly

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:07.680
what it is just yet, but
I want you to think about

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:12.260
what two consecutive whole
numbers is 18 divided by four,

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:14.563
whatever that is, what is that between?

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:17.700
Well, we could do something similar.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.470
We could say, all right, let's see,

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:22.530
four times four is equal to 16,

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.670
so that doesn't quite get us to 18.

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:29.590
We could say that four
times five is equal to 20,

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:31.480
so that's more than 18.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:36.360
So four times question
mark is equal to 18.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.160
This helps us realize that

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.410
because 18 is between 16 and 20,

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.370
this question mark
right over here is going

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:43.860
to be between four and five.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:48.700
So 18 divided by four is going
to be four point something.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:52.370
Now, another way of
thinking about or estimating

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:56.380
what division might result
in is through an inequality.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.720
So if I were to say 87

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:02.600
divided by nine,

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:06.690
how would you compare
that to 10 over here?

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.100
So there's a couple of
ways you could compare it.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.860
You could say, hey, maybe
this is greater than 10.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:12.850
Maybe it's equal to 10.

00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:15.150
Maybe it is less than 10.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:17.710
So pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:18.760
What would you put here?

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.573
Is it less than, greater
than, or equal to 10?

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.550
Well, we know it's not equal to 10.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:29.140
We know that 90 divided by nine

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.290
is equal to 10.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.960
And let's see, if we go one
multiple of nine less than that,

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:38.580
we know that 81 divided by nine

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:41.230
is equal to nine.

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:45.930
And so 87 divided by nine is
in between these two values.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:47.610
Let me do this in another color.

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:51.920
So 87 divided by nine is going

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:55.920
to be something in between nine and 10.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:00.920
And so it is going to be less than 10.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:03.370
So the whole point of
this video is to start

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:05.270
to get us a little bit comfortable

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:10.270
with this idea of dividing
where we might get an answer

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.320
that is not a whole number.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.390
And in the future we'll
learn how to compute that,

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:16.320
but for now we're just
learning to estimate

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:18.660
and just get a sense of, hey, okay,

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:21.120
this is going to be
between eight and nine.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:24.150
This is going to be between four and five.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:28.330
This is going to be between nine and 10,

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:30.730
which just means it's going
to be nine point something,

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:32.830
which means it's going to be less than 10.

